course: dictionary
lesson: 8947
title: Sill: a shelf, a step, or a layer of rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sill is a flat ledge. The one you meet most is the window sill, the shelf at the bottom of a window, where people keep plants or ornaments. «Mum put the cress on the sunny window sill.» Plants sit on a flat ledge, so a sill is a flat ledge.
explain: Read the words around sill to find out which meaning is meant. «The cat stepped over the door sill» is about a doorway, so the sill is the bottom part of a door frame. «A geologist found a sill of rock between two layers» is about rocks, so it means a flat layer of rock.
explain: The example from the story is playful: «The 'Stute Fish hides in the mud under the "Door-sills of the Equator".» The words are made up for a fanciful tale, but the clue is the same as before. A door sill is the bottom part of a door frame, so the phrase means the bottom of a doorway.
fact: A sill is a flat shelf or ledge.
fact: «Window sill» (also «windowsill») means the shelf at the bottom of a window.
fact: «Door sill» means the bottom part of a door frame, the bit you step over.
fact: In geology, a sill is a flat layer of rock that formed when hot melted rock pushed between other layers.
fact: Context clues tell you which meaning of a word is meant, so always read the sentence around it.
exercise: «Mia put her pot of cress on the sunny window sill.» Where did Mia put the cress? | Up a tree | Inside the fridge | *On a flat shelf at the bottom of a window | In a bag
exercise: «The cat stepped over the door sill.» What is a door sill? | *The bottom part of a door frame | The top of a door | A key | A kind of cat
exercise: «A geologist found a sill of rock between two layers.» What is a sill in this sentence? | A tall cliff | A river | *A flat layer of rock formed when hot melted rock pushed between other layers | A small stone
test: Which word is a good synonym for the shelf at the bottom of a window? | Door | Wall | *Ledge | Roof
test: «The 'Stute Fish hides in the mud under the "Door-sills of the Equator".» Which kind of sill is meant here? | A flat layer of rock | A river bank | A window shelf for plants | *The bottom part of a door frame
exam: «A bird landed on the window sill.» What does sill mean here? | The bottom part of a door frame | A wooden fence | *A flat shelf at the bottom of a window | A flat layer of rock
